                        "entry_id": "00253f74-2bbf-3419-b471-d01dcba324d1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Irritable; easily upset; angry; tending to complain."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "489f850b-e298-4a9a-99c6-5ef696aa8bda",
                                "sense_id": "88498e7b-5a4f-3bbd-bf1d-5fe170b9b6db",
                                "text": "His boss gets grouchy when deadlines draw near."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b7d9069f-8835-4bf9-9669-d6a38e96031f",
                                "sense_id": "88498e7b-5a4f-3bbd-bf1d-5fe170b9b6db",
                                "text": "Not that young Pat had a nasty temper, or was grouchy as his father had feared."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d9bf344d-0b15-4f05-9ba4-5a3a997371be",
                                "sense_id": "88498e7b-5a4f-3bbd-bf1d-5fe170b9b6db",
                                "text": "He went in to mumble that he was \"sorry, didn't mean to be grouchy,\" and to inquire as to her interest in movies."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dff0362f-9ad3-4146-a795-b4e1f1d4302d",
                                "sense_id": "88498e7b-5a4f-3bbd-bf1d-5fe170b9b6db",
                                "text": "In Berlin I once heard Susie Clemens—ill-fated, talented girl, who died so young—say to her father: \"Grouchy again! They do say that you can be funny when company is around—too bad that you don't consider Henry Fisher company.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
